;; The classes of diffcheck's Java forms' pair (bin/diffcheck, test/diffcheck/known.edn's cases
;; under test/j2g/: the Java forms interpreted against translated by j2g), a check beside Java's
;; eval level (doc/FULL-SUPPORT-SURVEY.md, REAP1; the level's own check is bin/java-check's interp,
;; JC1, test/java/divergences.edn), and of diffcheck's exclusions (test/diffcheck/jforms-excluded.edn:
;; the Java forms' classes diffcheck does not give j2g), a source beside Java's AOT level (RPS27 (a);
;; its own check is bin/java-check's compiled level, JC2). A case is "known REASON" or "excluded
;; REASON", matched as in test/goi/divergences.edn.
;; Read with the Clojure reader.
[
 {:id :interp-world-limits
  :title "the interpreter's known limits: a run-time class extending java.io.StringReader, java.lang.invoke's MethodHandles"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "a class of Java forms made at run time cannot extend java.io.StringReader (FxCode) nor reach MethodHandles (FxVarHandles); j2g translates both (test/j2g/record_fixtures.ae records the fixtures on the JVM for them). The world's classes (extendable superclasses, java.lang.invoke) are ranked by JC6 and each decided by the user (JCS9 (b), RPS8 (a)): not yet"
  :decided "RPS21 (a), deferred, decided with JC6's ranking (doc/FULL-SUPPORT-SURVEY.md, \"Decided (2026-10-24): RPS18-RPS29\")"
  :match [#"^known The Java forms' pair, the interpreter's known limits"]}
 {:id :jforms-namespace-body
  :title "diffcheck's exclusions: Clojure in a class body naming the namespace's vars or a deftype made in the body"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "j2g analyzes the Java forms without the namespace's vars and cannot name a class the evaluator makes at run time (dcf.defclass.Clj, native.nested_deftype.Host, cfcorpus.c11.ClojureData, cfcorpus.c16.F2): F2.4's kin, j2g's analysis of c2j's classes given the namespace's vars (RPS6 (a), REAP3)"
  :decided "RPS27 (a): F2.4's kin deferred to REAP3 (doc/FULL-SUPPORT-SURVEY.md, \"Decided (2026-10-24): RPS18-RPS29\")"
  :match [#"^excluded (Clojure in a class body|A deftype inside a class body)"]}
 {:id :jforms-corpus-own
  :title "diffcheck's exclusions: the Java forms compiler's corpus's own classes that fail in both halves"
  :kind :design
  :why "classes of the corpus that name what it does not define (clojure.lang.IDeref, another test file's classes), that its tests expect not to compile, or that declare a native method with no Go implementation: the interpreter fails to define them as j2g does"
  :decided "RPS27 (a): the corpus's own classes failing in both halves by design"
  :match [#"^excluded (Implements clojure\.lang\.IDeref|Its reify implements|defclass_corpus\.ae keeps|Classes the Java forms compiler's tests expect|Declares a native method)"]}
]
